These failure rate data show much larger term-to-term variation than the course GPAs, especially post-Covid. Math 16B (Calculus II for social scientists) certainly shows a striking increase in failures post-2020. However, presumably students in 16B either passed 16A at Berkeley or scored a minimum grade on an AP test; it's hard to see how this trend could be attributed to high school grade inflation or UC ending use of the SAT. 


